    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a `selfLink` field (`/api/owners/{id}`) to the owner representation. Two files touched, each edit minimal:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `getSelfLink`/`setSelfLink`.\n\n2. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** \u2014 one line: `dto.setSelfLink(\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId())`. This is the GET responder the test reads back through (`GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\nI kept structural impact low by putting the single line in the existing tiny responder class (its `service` method has CC=1 and no sibling methods, so `WMC_other`\u22480), rather than modifying a larger class or adding new pipeline steps. The `selfLink` is derived purely from the owner id at response time, so no entity, mapper, or persistence changes were needed.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsSelfLink` and the full suite pass.",
